# .vercelignore -- files EXCLUDED from the Vercel deployment.
# Source of truth: AL-MURABBI-MASTER.md section 13 (both lists measured).
# Everything below is build-time / reference only -- nothing the browser or a
# serverless function fetches at runtime.
# NEVER add here: index.html, sw.js, manifest.json, adhkar.json (root),
# quran-uthmani.json, mushaf-layout.json, icon-*.png, icon.svg, privacy.html,
# delete.html, worship-display.json, api/**, lib/**, package.json, package-lock.json,
# app.js, vendor/** (item 32: the page does not render without the last two)

# build + guard scripts (run on the dev machine, never in production)
tools/
guards/
worship-guard.cjs
quran-guard.cjs
layout-guard.cjs
quran-verify.cjs
build-mushaf-layout.cjs
build-worship-display.cjs
build-golden-md.cjs
esc.cjs
flip-stream-flag.cjs

# golden / reference data (read at BUILD time only)
quran-golden.json
referral-golden.json
golden-set-worship.md

# worship-golden.json: safe to exclude NOW -- the client fetches worship-display.json.
# defect 38: once the worship-strip (part two / defect 5b) lands, the client will
# need this at runtime. REMOVE the next line then, or the worship columns die.
# THE TRIGGER, NAMED: session 11 -- the live board. When the worship strip ships there, the line below goes.
worship-golden.json

# retired code kept only so the next reader can see what was tried and why it
# went. Nothing here is imported by anything -- that is the entry condition for
# moving a file in. It must never ship.
_superseded/

# source docs (public on GitHub, not served as pages), experiments, and the
# redundant data copy (the root adhkar.json is the one that ships)
docs/
spike/
lib/data/adhkar.json
.env*
babel-block.jsx

# ITEM 32. app.jsx is the SOURCE the shipped bundle is built from -- 1MB of JSX the browser
# never reads, because tools/build-app.cjs compiles it into app.js before the commit. Build
# time only, so it is excluded. app.js itself must NEVER be added here: it is the application.
app.jsx

# vendor/ IS NO LONGER EXCLUDED, and that line going was the point of item 32. React and
# ReactDOM are served from this origin now (index.html loads vendor/react.umd.js and
# vendor/react-dom.umd.js with an SRI hash cut over the local bytes) and sw.js precaches both.
# Excluding the directory would deploy a page that loads two scripts the deployment does not
# contain -- a 404 on each, and nothing renders at all. It belongs with index.html and sw.js
# in the NEVER-ADD list at the top of this file.
